jpg","c":"BACKPIECE(Ed. Lacey)---Chris Steer leads Charlie Dabbs during the \"Cecil Fry\" Trophy meeting '3'. They finished 5th and 3rd respectively with 14:28.0 and 14:22.4.","id":"B151-56","w":"August 1963"},{"f":"crops/B153/B153-p11-hart-steer-fairclough.jpg","c":"Hart, Steer & Fairclough","id":"B153-17","w":"April 1964"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p25-dance-with-team.jpg","c":"My picture shows Bill (far right) alongside Chris Steer, our President Bob Taylor, Trevor Hart and Alan Black; with the two Norths and Dabbs in the front row.","id":"B158-52","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p31-team-await-start.jpg","c":"CENTRE: A confident team await the start. (L to R): Black,Merry,Geoff North Gerry North,Dear,Steer,Major and Dabbs.","id":"B158-61","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p31-chris-steer.jpg","c":"BOTTOM RIGHT: Chris Steer, who was our 8th scorer.","id":"B158-61","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B158/B158-p35-chris-steer-mitcham-15.jpg","c":"A fine study by two fine photographers(Ed Lacey and Ron Linstead) of a fine athlete. Chris Steer in action during the Mitcham '15'.","id":"B158-66","w":"March 1966"},{"f":"crops/B161/B161-p29-steer-brew-mitcham-15.jpg","c":"'Chris Steer (right) and' Doug Brew (left) seem to find running in the Mitcham '15' highly amusing. The joke wore a bit thin though for Chris was later forced to retire!","id":"B161-43","w":"March 1967"},{"f":"crops/B163/B163-p32-mann-steer.jpg","c":"BOTTOM CENTRE: Lionel Mann and Chris Steer having their usual private duel.","id":"B163-81","w":"September 1967"},{"f":"crops/B164/B164-p10-relay-montage.jpg","c":"PHOTOS:(R.Linstead)---Brian Buxton hands over to Chris Steer in the Walton Relay (top). Peter Whewell (A23) sets off for a fast lap in the Belgrave Relay while Buxton (A4) is seen finishing second on the first stage. No.64 is Our President who, by running in the Yacht handicap during his year of office, probably made history.","id":"B164-16","w":"December 1967"},{"f":"crops/B164/B164-p14-steer-north-handover.jpg","c":"LEFT:Chris Steer sends Gerry North off with a good lead.","id":"B164-22","w":"December 1967"},{"f":"crops/B166/B166-p06-steer-rimmer-tvh-relay.jpg","c":"Chris Steer hands over to Jim Rimmer in the T.V.H. Relay at Cranford","id":"B166-08","w":"June 1968"},{"f":"crops/B177/B177-p16-road-race-runners.jpg","c":"The 5¾-miles championship field, still hunched after one mile. Front row: Pat O'Connor (12), Tony Fairclough (21), Peter Carton (19), Trevor Hart (23), and Lionel Mann (9). The three framed heads look like those of Chris Steer, John Thresher and Dereck Fernee.","id":"B177-34","w":"June 1971"},{"f":"crops/B202/B202-p29-chris-steer.jpg","c":"Chris Steer runs the fastest leg in the Cranford Relay to Qualify for our Southern Relay Team.","id":"B202-88","w":"April 1981"},{"f":"crops/B226/B226-p18-dinner-enjoying.jpg","c":"Left: Enjoying the occasion.  Pat Mead, Tony Binda, Marianne Black, Gerry North, Alan Black, the late Laurie O'Hara, George Piddington, Charlie Henn, Ted Pallant, Chris Steer, Charlie Manning.\n\nSadly this was the last time that we saw Laurie O'Hara.  He died the following day while out running.","id":"B226-40","w":"March 1998"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B147/B147-p11-ramble-faygate.jpg","caption":"The above photograph was taken last January, on a ramble which started from Faygate,Sussex and shows Barry Sawyer, Ron 'Ozog' Langheim,Derek Crookes Mike Shingles, Chris Steer, and Bob Taylor.","source":"B147-18","when":"May 1962"},"slarchive":"https://slarchive.org/#athlete/chris-steer","slRaces":12,"x":1,"legend":false}